libfprint-elan-0c6e-fix for Ubuntu
---------------------------------

This companion package installs a device-specific udev rule for USB device
04f3:0c6e. It is intended for the locally patched Ubuntu 26.04 libfprint
1:1.95.1+tod1-0ubuntu1.1 packages supplied in the same bundle.

The protocol patch prevents the device's 0xaf finger-present response from
aborting capture. This package handles the independent USB runtime-suspend
disconnection.

The reader remains exposed as a swipe device. Native tap images are too small
for libfprint's current NBIS matcher, and verification quality remains dependent
on swipe angle and speed.

 -- Sikander Khan <skhan1903@outlook.com>, July 2026
